<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Trimmer roots for the Blazor WASM client (IsTrimmable=true → Release builds trim IL).

  THE ROUTING BUG (why the whole assembly is preserved):
  Blazor's <Router> discovers routable page components (@page "/…") purely by
  reflecting over the app assembly for [Route] attributes and then instantiates
  them *reflectively* via DefaultComponentActivator. The trimmer cannot see that
  reflective use, so in the trimmed Release build it removes every page component
  that nothing else references statically — which is ALL of them. With no page
  types left, the Router registers no routes and falls through to <NotFound> for
  every path, including "/". The user sees the MainLayout chrome (rooted below,
  historically) wrapping "Sorry, there's nothing at this address."

  This is the same class of bug as the earlier MainLayout CtorNotLocated failure:

      System.InvalidOperationException: CtorNotLocated,
      PoMiniGamesClient.Layout.MainLayout

  reflectively-used members look dead to the trimmer and only break in Azure
  (local Debug builds are not trimmed). Rather than enumerate ~50 page types by
  hand — and silently break every time a new game page is added — we preserve the
  whole client assembly. Framework/library assemblies are still trimmed for size;
  only this app assembly (the one the Router reflects over) is kept intact. This
  supersedes the earlier per-type MainLayout root.

  NOTE: this only affects runtime IL preservation. EnableTrimAnalyzer in the
  csproj still runs at build time, so trim-unsafe patterns are still flagged.
  This is the runtime counterpart to the IL2110/IL2111 suppressions there.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="PoMiniGamesClient" preserve="all" />
</linker>
